#
# Faster batch-invariant mHC and rank-order reduce, bitwise unchanged.
#
# - The FP32 rank-order sum of patch 10 runs as one Triton kernel with the same
#   left-to-right FP32 adds and one rounding (~28 us -> ~2.4 us per call at 8
#   ranks).
# - TileLang mHC pre-norm GEMM uses the block-M kernel with the same K order and
#   reductions.
#
# Upstream: the reduce matches #52231's fixed-order sum kernel except for the
# sign of an all-(-0) sum and NaN payloads; the mHC part belongs to the
# DeepSeek-V4 ROCm RFC.
#
# Source commits:
#   [ROCm][BI] Faster batch-invariant mHC and rank-order reduce, bitwise unchanged
#
